            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-40] BookieClientTest fails intermittantly</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-40</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;To repro:&lt;br/&gt;
true; while [ $? = 0 ]; do mvn test -Dtest=BookieClientTest; done&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Problem seems to be&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;        BookieClient bc = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; BookieClient(channelFactory, executor);
        ChannelBuffer bb;
        bb = createByteBuffer(1, 1, 1);
        bc.addEntry(addr, 1, passwd, 1, bb, wrcb, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;);
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;synchronized&lt;/span&gt; (arc) {
            bc.readEntry(addr, 1, 1, recb, arc);

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The test doesn&apos;t wait for addEntry to complete before doing a read. It should be simple to fix. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
